   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to admission requirements for\ngraduate-level teacher and educational leader programs",
    "basePrintNo": "S7118",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7118-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 18,
       "fullName": "Julia Salazar",
       "imgName": "1047_Julia_Salazar.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1227,
       "sessionMemberId": 1225,
       "sessionYear": 2019,
       "shortName": "SALAZAR"
      }
     ],
     "size": 1
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §210-a, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S7118\n\nSPONSOR: SANDERS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to admission requirements\nfor graduate-level teacher and educational leader programs\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo provide higher education institutions with alternative criteria to\nuse in determining admission into graduate-level and educational leader\nprograms.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1. Amends section 210-a of the Education Law to provide higher\neducation institutions with alternative admission requirements for grad-\nuate-Level teacher and educational leader programs.\n\nSection 2. Provides for an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPrior to the enactment of provisions contained in chapter 56 of the Laws\nof 2015, higher education institutions had the full discretion and\nautonomy to consider multiple measures when determining whether or not\nto admit a student into their graduate-level and educational leader\nprograms. The requirement that a student have an overall GPA of 3.0 is a\none-size fits all policy that prohibits educational institutions from\napplying discretion to identifying an individual's potential quality as\na future teacher.\n\nThis legislation will provide higher education institutions with more\ndiscretion through the expansion of criteria to be used when considering\nwhether or not to admit a student into their program.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017-18: A10952 Passed Assembly\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
